# Test-run pollution: #72 already removed the production prediction-ledger
# write path, so any growth here is local pytest runs, not real usage
# (measured: ~14.5KB per test, quadratic -- see tests/conftest.py). The NHL/
# MLB/soccer odds-lifecycle tests independently leak into the real repo's
# data/odds_events/<date>.jsonl the same way; both got swept into 0250ac82
# by accident.
data/prediction_ledger.json
data/odds_events/

# tests/test_mlb_refresh_runner.py's live-lens tests mock live_lens_report_path
# to a bare relative "report.json" instead of a tmp path; repeatedly leaked
# fixture output into this repo-root file across several sessions (66720d0b,
# 42472a9f, 71b57a82, ...) and got committed by accident each time.
/report.json

# Session-local hook markers, not shared ledger state. `/lane open` writes the
# current slug so lane-guard.py can tell this session's claims from another
# session's; `/checkpoint` touches the second so checkpoint-guard.sh can tell
# persisted work from lost work. Both are per-machine, per-session.
.syndicate/.current-lane
.syndicate/.last-checkpoint
# Liveness marker for the hourly `unknown-submit-balance-evidence-capture`
# task. Overwritten each run, never appended, and deliberately NOT committed:
# it answers a LOCAL question (did this machine run it recently) and hourly
# commits would be the noise the task's silence exists to avoid. Ignored so it
# cannot be swept into another session's `git add` from the shared tree.
.syndicate/.unknown_submit_watch_heartbeat*

# Deploy claims are runtime state about RIGHT NOW, not history. A claim in git
# would be a claim that outlives its truth.
.syndicate/deploy_claims/

# Per-session lane markers. The single-valued .current-lane could not represent
# N concurrent sessions, so each session now writes its own; they are runtime
# state about who holds what RIGHT NOW, not history.
.syndicate/.current-lane.*

# Test-run and local-runtime output (`#502` session, 2026-08-22). Each of these
